      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_8e3659b328b48baad7b5a4868eb0fe625d2b8d113935c36763e54f01235db4ef",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Phase-amplitude separation isolates exponential growth from prefactors, while frequency decomposition changes one oscillatory integral into a finite competition among saddles. Algebraizing the saddle equation makes admissible critical points classifiable rather than chosen heuristically.",
