    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2a0d21b22b54b96d95f2e870842f843c2faf51737b2f62557ffa34c101135591",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Reflection oddness of the rational function filters the partial-fraction expansion to a controlled band of odd zeta values before asymptotic estimation. The differentiated cotangent kernel then represents that already filtered discrete derivative sum as a vertical contour integral, preserving the same linear form in a representation suitable for saddle analysis. Thus the arithmetic support restriction precedes, and is carried into, the analytic phase.",
