    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9563e6b97160e350f00dece3f1c39a89d90d2f3554e67e67d3ca817a04d28b34",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In this construction, the final deductions come from comparing separately established exponential budgets. For finite-panel irrationality, the prime-adic denominator saving and normalization cost are combined with the magnitude rate κ of the linear form in a strict negativity condition. For linear-independence and dimension bounds, the coefficient-growth estimate supplies an additional cost under a cited independence criterion. The parameters therefore control both which odd zeta values occur and whether the relevant rate comparison succeeds.",
