    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d0c334f84b988565e66691e6fa4b9ae7c24ccb59aedc20b26fdbd4464138064a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The odd parameters a, b, and c jointly design the construction: a and b determine the supported band b<s<a+b of odd zeta values, while all three parameters affect the denominator and asymptotic rates that must satisfy the final criterion. Explicit triples and parameter families are then chosen so that the support covers the theorem's finite panels and the strict rate inequality holds. The resulting panel statements assert that at least one member is irrational; they do not select which member. In the b=1 branch, further choices combined with a cited independence criterion yield dimension lower bounds.",
